# vehje-runtime-abi — backlog

## Deferred ABI type surface

- Full `AbiSpan` wrapping `vehje_ir::FileId` + `ByteOffset`
  (skeleton ships a flat `{ file, start, end }` triple).
- `AbiToken` mirror for `vehje_ir::Token`.
- `AbiNode` mirror for `vehje_ir::Node`.
- `From` impls between vehje-ir types and their `Abi*`
  mirrors (one direction: vehje-ir → Abi for outgoing data;
  Abi → vehje-ir for incoming diagnostics).
- `abi_version: u32` prefix on every public struct — carries
  the ABI-version invariant R2 mandates.
- Flip bare-primitive FFI-wire sites to `UWire<N>`. Current
  policy keeps `i32` / `u32` scalars on the C-ABI boundary
  bare with `lint:allow(arvo-types-only) tracked: #207` where
  no arvo newtype provides wire-identical layout. A future
  `arvo::UWire<N>` (see arvo BACKLOG) is a fixed-width wire-
  stable newtype without the `S: Strategy` axis. When it
  lands, every bare-primitive FFI site in this crate flips.

## Deferred entry points

- `vehje_runtime_init(arena_bytes: u32)` — per-session arena
  allocation.
- `vehje_runtime_shutdown(handle)` — teardown entry.
- `vehje_runtime_invoke_macro(handle, nodes, len)` — macro
  dispatch surface.
- `vehje_runtime_eval_scratch(handle, expr_nodes, len)` —
  compile-time scratch evaluation.
- `vehje_runtime_expand_generative(handle, blueprint, len)` —
  generative subgraph expansion.
- `vehje_runtime_last_error(handle) -> *const AbiDiagnostic`
  — retrieve the last-recorded error diagnostic.

## Deferred framework features

- **Full `ClauseRuntime` state struct.** Currently opaque
  `[u8; 0]`; future round fills in the real state body when
  the runtime backend lands.
- **Real `vehje_runtime_execute` wiring.** Currently returns
  `Err`. Future round hands off to a loaded runtime dylib via
  the driver-side dispatch.
- **Error code → `ClauseDiagnostic` translation layer.** When
  execute returns an error, surface the associated diagnostic
  via `vehje_runtime_last_error`.
- **Panic handling at FFI boundary.** Wrap every `extern "C"`
  body in `std::panic::catch_unwind` (once std is acceptable
  here; currently `no_std`) or via an explicit abort guard
  so a Rust panic never unwinds into Zig.
- **Thread safety guarantees on the ABI.** Document what's
  `Send` vs `Sync`. Decision: handle is `!Send + !Sync` per
  session, driver wraps in `Arc<Mutex<>>` if shared; real
  answer lives in the next round.
- **Little-endian guard.** Refuse big-endian loads via a
  startup compile-time / init-time check.

## Non-blocking follow-ups

- C header generation (`cbindgen` run during build).
- Stable ABI versioning tag — bumped on every breaking change.
- Cross-platform calling-convention audit (stdcall vs cdecl
  on Windows is the usual hazard).
